{"title":"1950 AHSME Problems/Problem 49","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Complex_Numbers)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Complex Numbers)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_49&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A triangle has a fixed base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> inches long. The median from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/4/824e8063e0e98377ca5f38b4a59b3729d307fd57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> inches long and can have any position emanating from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. The locus of the vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> of the triangle is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/c/32c861d19f0f347642a03410cee6ab9f5427511d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{A straight line }AB,1\\dfrac{1}{2}\\text{ inches from }A \\qquad\\\\ \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{A circle with }A\\text{ as center and radius }2\\text{ inches} \\qquad\\\\ \\textbf{(C)}\\  \\text{A circle with }A\\text{ as center and radius }3\\text{ inches} \\qquad\\\\ \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{A circle with radius }3\\text{ inches and center }4\\text{ inches from }B\\text{ along } BA \\qquad\\\\ \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{An ellipse with }A\\text{ as focus}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"526\" height=\"114\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_49&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The locus of the median's endpoint on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is the circle about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/4/824e8063e0e98377ca5f38b4a59b3729d307fd57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> inches.  The locus of the vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is then the circle twice as big and twice as far from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, i.e. of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> inches and with center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> inches from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> along <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/6/d66492998689e8303534c9e4f3ba1fa650fd41f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> which means that our answer is: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b305929a95b53f14a0ad53eba1d8560626e1f28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_49&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/b/7bbf9b82b34a0adc8319d2e58f610e214294c21a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A(a,y_A)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/2/c32d98c74dd8f0e8a4e481642a43672add41f8bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B(b,y_B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/9/8b90c2d963ad6794060e1af0ec699535f6f4fb59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c44e86239496410e9e2c156d57b9f8a6437c2181.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D\\left(\\frac{x+b}{2},\\frac{y+y_B}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"150\" height=\"43\" /> is a midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the equation of needed locus is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/1/8b107cf25ef1a86da1ab76ededbfbb0935c23a49.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\frac{x+b}{2}-a\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{y+y_B}{2}-y_A\\right)^2=\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2,\\]\" width=\"338\" height=\"46\" />\nwhich is equation of the circle:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/a/41a4c4a789bf630a348a4fecb8ef3ebbfb417eba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x-(2a-b))^2+(y-(2y_A-y_B))^2=3^2.\\]\" width=\"321\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Thus, D) is valid because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/1/8d1cf2f95352488d9fe02195dada98d3927eb496.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{(2a-b-b)^2+(2y_A-y_B-y_B)^2}=2\\sqrt{(a-b)^2+(y_A-y_b)^2}=2AB=4.\\]\" width=\"586\" height=\"32\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Complex_Numbers.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Complex_Numbers)\">Solution 3 (Complex Numbers)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_49&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Complex Numbers)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Place <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> in the complex plane such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/4/724073a282d1ae8d072d84c4618bf6275c1d5ae9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = 0$\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed45766ae06d282b582b4b49d4289dcc81331314.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = 2$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75df875d5a3fda6da7f15821fbe3a383bf7e4cef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM = 1.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />, the locus of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/a/2ea74789f9d513896fa2d2f502746b631b344c01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.5z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> over all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/1/83147269611ed30c50eb2ddeb1b275003b3ab032.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z| = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a1948f1518384ec1d0b7f265d415b5b6ad8f5991.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M = \\frac{B+C}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"101\" height=\"39\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/9/6f95aa2195fd53458f0e67d68cd8abd90bcc0f4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = 2M-B = 3z-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"180\" height=\"16\" />.  Therefore, the locus of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is a circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/a/62a76677add1d246708c86edfc7c4b8a40184914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> units from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> along <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/6/d66492998689e8303534c9e4f3ba1fa650fd41f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />, thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/7/127d931522545e051568ec39722570e4dd63005e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(\\textbf{D})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"40\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p><p>-j314andrews\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_49&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l4lAvs2P_YA&amp;t=333s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l4lAvs2P_YA&amp;t=333s</a>\n</p><p>~MathProblemSolvingSkills.com\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_49&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME\" title=\"1950 AHSME\">1950 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1950 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1950 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1950\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_48\" title=\"1950 AHSME Problems/Problem 48\">Problem 48</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_50\" title=\"1950 AHSME Problems/Problem 50\">Problem 50</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1950 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1950 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1950 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1950 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1950 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1950 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1950 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1950 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1950_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1950 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a hre